WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.394
A clock tells you when. A
compass tells you which way.

2
00:00:08.614 --> 00:00:12.190
Today you will use both, and
work out how long things take.

3
00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.987
A clock has two hands, and
they do different jobs.

4
00:00:16.207 --> 00:00:21.130
The long hand gives the minutes. Each
number it passes is five minutes.

5
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:26.040
The short hand gives the hour.
Read the number it has just passed.

6
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:31.415
The long hand is at 3, and the short
hand has passed 3. Quarter past three.

7
00:00:31.635 --> 00:00:37.533
Now the long hand moves to 6. Half past three,
and the short hand has crept halfway to 4.

8
00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:43.420
A time is a point in the day. A time
interval is how long something lasts.

9
00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.866
A film starts at 10:40 and
ends at 11:15. How long is it?

10
00:00:48.086 --> 00:00:53.241
Do not take one time from the other. An
hour is sixty minutes, not a hundred.

11
00:00:53.461 --> 00:00:57.269
Count on instead. 10:40 to
11:00 is twenty minutes.

12
00:00:57.489 --> 00:01:04.037
Then 11:00 to 11:15 is fifteen more.
Twenty and fifteen make 35 minutes.

13
00:01:04.257 --> 00:01:10.340
It works for weeks too. 2 weeks
is 7 days, then 7 more: 14 days.

14
00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:16.088
Some things take seconds. Others
take minutes, hours, days or years.

15
00:01:16.308 --> 00:01:21.556
Amina walks to school. Is that 15
seconds, 15 minutes or 15 hours?

16
00:01:21.776 --> 00:01:25.444
15 seconds is far too quick.
You would not reach the gate.

17
00:01:25.664 --> 00:01:29.473
15 hours is far too long.
That is most of a day.

18
00:01:29.693 --> 00:01:35.172
15 minutes fits. Picture the thing
happening, then choose the unit.

19
00:01:35.672 --> 00:01:39.202
A timetable sets out
times in rows and columns.

20
00:01:39.422 --> 00:01:42.998
Each column is one bus.
Each row is one stop.

21
00:01:43.218 --> 00:01:46.933
Hodan must be at the Library
by 10 o'clock. Which bus?

22
00:01:47.153 --> 00:01:53.144
Find the Library row, and keep a finger
on it. Bus 3 arrives at 10:10, too late.

23
00:01:53.364 --> 00:01:57.590
Bus 2 arrives at 9:45,
so Hodan catches Bus 2.

24
00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:01.712
North, south, east and west
are the four cardinal points.

25
00:02:01.932 --> 00:02:04.811
On a map, north is up and south is down.

26
00:02:05.031 --> 00:02:07.957
East is to the right,
and west is to the left.

27
00:02:08.177 --> 00:02:12.124
Your left and right change when
you turn. North never does.

28
00:02:12.344 --> 00:02:17.871
Clockwise is the way a clock's hands
go. Anticlockwise is the other way.

29
00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:21.157
Here is a map. Amina starts at the Home.

30
00:02:21.377 --> 00:02:25.046
Go 2 squares east, which
is 2 squares to the right.

31
00:02:25.266 --> 00:02:28.981
Then go 2 squares north,
which is 2 squares up the map.

32
00:02:29.201 --> 00:02:34.310
Amina reaches the School. Say those
words and anyone can follow them.

33
00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:38.291
Face west, turn a quarter turn
clockwise, and you face north.

34
00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:43.110
The short hand gives the hour, and
the long hand gives the minutes.

35
00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:46.813
Count on to find how long,
and choose a unit that fits.

36
00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:52.467
Read a timetable by row and column.
North, south, east and west never move.
